    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0244" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/891a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Ambassador to
                        Great Britain</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 17, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A report comes from the American representatives at the London conference that
                    there has been a failure to reach an agreement with Russia and Japan as to
                    participating in the Chinese loan. Ascertain the real difficulties and the
                    attitude of the British Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
